 by the last attack  and without his supreme generation he's  struggling to breathe  the number one hero says that shiguraki  can never bring down hero society  because his destruction is hollow and  it's not supported  by any ideals that said the villain  replies by repeating something that he  heard from his father  when he was young which is that heroes  hurt their own families  just to help strangers this statement is  very applicable to endeavour  who of course brought his wife to the  brink of insanity not to mention gave a  terrible childhood  to virtually all of his children shiggy  begins to stand up  and says that whilst heroes pretend to  be society's guardians  in reality they ignore people that they  can't protect  with the scene then flashing back to a  young tenko shimura  wandering alone in the streets of japan  he goes on to elaborate  that hero society is rotten from the  core and that people have become so  dependent on heroes that they neglect to  do the right thing  for themselves this was implied by the  flashback that you can see on screen  in which an old lady sees a young tenko  but decides not to do anything because  she assumes  a hero or the police will deal with it  according to shigaraki  the system has always rejected him and  so now he's rejecting it back  which is the reason he took the power of  all for one in his words  he doesn't care if the heroes understand  him or not because this difference in  understanding is what makes them heroes  and villains  and that my friends is the end of part 3  of this war arc review  if you'd like to see my face reveal and  also how you can win some free  merchandise  then click on the video on screen and in  the description which will take you to  that face reveal  as always thank you for watching and  until the next one  peace out
 

